WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Fuel as a mixture. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Distinguish octane model from pump gasoline

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Commercial gasoline is a blend. Octane is a representative molecule often used for a simplified chemistry example.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: When a model writes C₈H₁₈, label it “octane model,” not “the exact contents of a fuel tank.”

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Claim check

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Material category alone does not guarantee strength, durability or safety.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Distinguish octane model from pump gasoline
